{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! In 2.9.0, `api_jwt.decode_complete` still has `if options[\"verify_signature\"] and not algorithms: raise DecodeError(...)`. Wait, that means `jwt.decode(token, key=pyjwk)` without algorithms would raise DecodeError from api_jwt.decode_complete?!\n\nHmm, wait. Let me re-check. In PyJWT 2.9.0... Let me test this directly. Let me install the 2.9.0 wheel into a temp venv or just run python with that wheel's jwt package on the path and test:\n\n```python\nimport jwt\nkey = jwt.PyJWK({\"kty\": \"oct\", \"k\": \"...\", \"alg\": \"HS256\"})\njwt.decode(token, key=key)\n```\n\nLet me check with the actual 2.9.0 wheel. Also let me check the tests in the 2.9.0 sdist to see the expected behavior. The sdist contains tests. Let me download the sdist.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Interesting! In 2.9.0, `api_jwt.decode_complete` still has `if options[\\\"verify_signature\\\"] and not algorithms: raise DecodeError(...)`. Wait, that means `jwt.decode(token, key=pyjwk)` without algorithms would raise DecodeError from api_jwt.decode_complete?!\\n\\nHmm, wait. Let me re-check. In PyJWT 2.9.0... Let me test this directly. Let me install the 2.9.0 wheel into a temp venv or just run python with that wheel's jwt package on the path and test:\\n\\n```python\\nimport jwt\\nkey = jwt.PyJWK({\\\"kty\\\": \\\"oct\\\", \\\"k\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"alg\\\": \\\"HS256\\\"})\\njwt.decode(token, key=key)\\n```\\n\\nLet me check with the actual 2.9.0 wheel. Also let me check the tests in the 2.9.0 sdist to see the expected behavior. The sdist contains tests. Let me download the sdist.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Interesting — in 2.9.0, `api_jwt.decode_complete` still has the `not algorithms` check. Let me verify actual behavior with the upstream wheel and check the upstream tests:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8215555521c646e2b8daa477","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp && PYTHONPATH=/tmp/pyjwt290 python3 -c \"\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '/tmp/pyjwt290')\nimport jwt\nprint(jwt.__version__)\nimport base64, json\ndef b64(d): return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(json.dumps(d).encode()).rstrip(b'=').decode()\nkey = jwt.PyJWK({'kty':'oct','k':'c2VjcmV0','alg':'HS256'})\nprint('alg name:', key.algorithm_name)\ntoken = jwt.encode({'some':'payload'}, 'secret', algorithm='HS256')\n# decode with PyJWK directly, no algorithms arg\nprint(jwt.decode(token, key=key))\nprint(jwt.decode_complete(token, key=key))\n\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_68a9dddaa0a04cfebf5183b6","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pip download pyjwt==2.9.0 --no-deps --no-binary :all: -d /tmp/pyjwt_sdist 2>&1 | tail -1; cd /tmp/pyjwt_sdist && tar xzf *.tar.gz && grep -rn \"algorithm_name\\|PyJWK\" PyJWT-2.9.0/tests/test_api_jwt.py | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":2651,"output":505,"cacheRead":18816,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":208,"totalTokens":21972,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788494213174,"responseId":"gen-1788494213-A3y6EAFNsqTyICDm8Xbv","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8215555521c646e2b8daa477","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 12, in <module>\n  File \"/tmp/pyjwt290/jwt/api_jwt.py\", line 211, in decode\n    decoded = self.decode_complete(\n  File \"/tmp/pyjwt290/jwt/api_jwt.py\", line 148, in decode_complete\n    raise DecodeError(\njwt.exceptions.DecodeError: It is required that you pass in a value for the \"algorithms\" argument when calling decode().\n2.9.0\nalg name: HS256\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1788494238869},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_68a9dddaa0a04cfebf