{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The 2.9.0 release actually raises DecodeError when calling `jwt.decode(token, key=pyjwk)` without algorithms! That was apparently a bug in 2.9.0 that was fixed in a later version (2.10.0?).\n\nWait, let me check. In PyJWT 2.9.0:\n- `api_jwt.decode_complete` still raises DecodeError if `not algorithms` — even when key is PyJWK.\n\nHmm, but wait — the PR #891 was supposed to make this work. Let me check if there was a follow-up fix. Actually yes! In PyJWT 2.10.0, there's:\n\n```python\n        if options[\"verify_signature\"] and not algorithms and not isinstance(key, PyJWK):\n            raise DecodeError(...)\n```\n\nLet me check the 2.10.1 code. Actually wait, let me check git history of api_jwt.py. The fix commit: \"fix: allow PyJWK to be passed to jwt.decode without algorithms\" or similar. Let me check 2.10.0.\n\nActually, let me check the sdist for tests — the sdist didn't include tests? Let me look at what's in it.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Interesting! The 2.9.0 release actually raises DecodeError when calling `jwt.decode(token, key=pyjwk)` without algorithms! That was apparently a bug in 2.9.0 that was fixed in a later version (2.10.0?).\\n\\nWait, let me check. In PyJWT 2.9.0:\\n- `api_jwt.decode_complete` still raises DecodeError if `not algorithms` — even when key is PyJWK.\\n\\nHmm, but wait — the PR #891 was supposed to make this work. Let me check if there was a follow-up fix. Actually yes! In PyJWT 2.10.0, there's:\\n\\n```python\\n        if options[\\\"verify_signature\\\"] and not algorithms and not isinstance(key, PyJWK):\\n            raise DecodeError(...)\\n```\\n\\nLet me check the 2.10.1 code. Actually wait, let me check git history of api_jwt.py. The fix commit: \\\"fix: allow PyJWK to be passed to jwt.decode without algorithms\\\" or similar. Let me check 2.10.0.\\n\\nActually, let me check the sdist for tests — the sdist didn't include tests? Let me look at what's in it.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The 2.9.0 release had a bug where `jwt.decode(token, key=pyjwk)` without algorithms still raised DecodeError. Let me check how this was fixed in later versions:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8741fa55061d4d408c2e1b9d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls /tmp/pyjwt_sdist/PyJWT-2.9.0/ && pip download pyjwt==2.10.1 --no-deps -d /tmp/pyjwt_ref2 2>&1 | tail -1 && cd /tmp && mkdir -p pyjwt2101 && cd pyjwt2101 && unzip -o -q /tmp/pyjwt_ref2/*.whl && grep -n \"not algorithms\" jwt/api_jwt.py jwt/api_jws.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":691,"output":406,"cacheRead":21440,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":257,"totalTokens":22537,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788494238870,"responseId":"gen-1788494238-36HIOlC1hkUATLkysUHz","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
