{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The upstream PR left `signing_algos = oidc_config[\"id_token_signing_alg_values_supported\"]` in place (the docs diff in PR #886 only removed the `algorithms=signing_algos` line, keeping the variable — since the OIDC server may support multiple algorithms and the JWK carries the right one). I'll keep it consistent with upstream: leave the variable as-is. It's an illustrative example; keeping it matches upstream exactly.\n\nNow, verify the final state of the modified source files, then update the tests per the PR (tests/test_api_jwk.py and tests/test_api_jws.py). Let me view the diffs so far.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The upstream PR left `signing_algos = oidc_config[\\\"id_token_signing_alg_values_supported\\\"]` in place (the docs diff in PR #886 only removed the `algorithms=signing_algos` line, keeping the variable — since the OIDC server may support multiple algorithms and the JWK carries the right one). I'll keep it consistent with upstream: leave the variable as-is. It's an illustrative example; keeping it matches upstream exactly.\\n\\nNow, verify the final state of the modified source files, then update the tests per the PR (tests/test_api_jwk.py and tests/test_api_jws.py). Let me view the diffs so far.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"That matches the upstream PR exactly (it kept the `signing_algos` config line). Now let me verify the source changes and run a quick functional check:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_145bca9e7e5f4410a1e92162","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /testbed && git diff jwt/"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_da4429fa00be4153a6f2fb4e","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /testbed && python -c \"\nimport jwt, base64, json\n\ndef b64(d): return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(json.dumps(d).encode()).rstrip(b'=').decode()\n\n# HS256 JWK\njwk = jwt.PyJWK({'kty':'oct','k':'c2VjcmV0','alg':'HS256'})\nprint('algorithm_name:', jwk.algorithm_name)\n\ntoken = jwt.encode({'some':'payload'}, 'secret', algorithm='HS256')\n\n# 1. jwt.decode with PyJWK and explicit algorithms\nprint('explicit alg:', jwt.decode(token, key=jwk, algorithms=['HS256']))\n# 2. jwt.decode with PyJWK, no algorithms -> uses JWK alg\nprint('implicit alg:', jwt.decode(token, key=jwk))\n# 3. decode_complete with PyJWK, no algorithms\nprint('complete:', jwt.decode_complete(token, key=jwk))\n# 4. mismatched header alg -> InvalidAlgorithmError\nbad = b64({'typ':'JWT','alg':'HS384'}) + '.' + token.split('.')[1] + '.' + token.split('.')[2]\ntry:\n    jwt.decode(bad, key=jwk)\n    print('ERROR: should have raised')\nexcept jwt.InvalidAlgorithmError as e:\n    print('mismatch raises InvalidAlgorithmError:', e)\n# 5. string key without algorithms still raises\ntry:\n    jwt.decode(token, 'secret')\nexcept jwt.DecodeError as e:\n    print('string key still requires algorithms:', e)\n# 6. PyJWS level\nimport jwt.api_jws as api_jws\npayload = api_jws.decode(token.encode(), jwk)\nprint('jws-level decode:', payload)\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":581,"output":560,"cacheRead":40640,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":139,"totalTokens":41781,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788494539762,"responseId":"gen-1788494539-EbOJNrkXPMxrzJMcJTAO","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_145bca9e7e5f4410a1e92162","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/jwt/api_jwk.py b/jwt/api_jwk.py\nindex af74578..d35b955 100644\n--- a/jwt/api_jwk.py\n+++ b/jwt/api_jwk.py\n@@ -52,9 +52,11 @@ class PyJWK:\n         if not has_crypto and algorithm in requires_cryptography:\n             raise PyJWKError(f\"{algorithm} requires 'cryptography' to be installed.\")\n \n-        self.Algorithm = self._algorithms.get(alg